PATCH 163: FUN_0000_1996 (asm 0x1996) -- the model-struct field initializer on the LOD model-load
path (reached BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT via 4308 -> 183f -> 1996), a pure DGROUP base-loss (the same class
as its neighbours 18dc/197b).  ES=DS=DGROUP; bx=word[DGROUP:0x2674] (the raw value of DAT_1000_e674,
which Ghidra mis-typed `int**`), di=word[DGROUP:(uint16)(bx+0x27f4)] = the model-struct near-offset,
then a fan-out broadcast of the struct words.  Ghidra dropped the DGROUP base so `*(DAT_1000_e674 +
0x27f4)` was a wild host-pointer dereference (SIGSEGV, gdb-confirmed at FUN_0000_1996+35).  The
recovered fan-out logic is otherwise instruction-faithful (verified vs the asm 0x1996..0x19b8); only
the base is rebased through g_mem+0x1c000 here.  Behaviour-neutral for verify (model-loader path,
unreached by the 19 flows -- a bare host deref there would already have SIGSEGV'd them).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -7815,8 +7815,17 @@
   undefined2 uVar3;
   int iVar4;
   undefined2 *puVar5;
-  
-  puVar2 = (undefined2 *)*(undefined2 *)(DAT_1000_e674 + 0x27f4);
+  /* PATCH 163 (asm 0x1996): ES=DS=DGROUP; every ptr here is a DGROUP near-offset, not a host ptr.
+     bx = word[DGROUP:0x2674] (the raw value of DAT_1000_e674, which Ghidra mis-typed int**);
+     di = word[DGROUP:(uint16)(bx+0x27f4)] = the model-struct near-offset -> rebase to g_mem+0x1c000.
+     The fan-out logic Ghidra recovered is correct; only the base was dropped (a wild host deref =
+     the SIGSEGV).  Model-loader path 4308->183f->1996; not reached by the 19 verify flows. */
+  {
+    unsigned char *dg = g_mem + 0x1c000;
+    uint16_t bx = *(uint16_t *)(dg + 0x2674);
+    uint16_t di = *(uint16_t *)(dg + (uint16_t)(bx + 0x27f4));
+    puVar2 = (undefined2 *)(dg + di);
+  }
   uVar1 = *puVar2;
   puVar2[1] = uVar1;
   puVar5 = puVar2 + 3;
